course: dictionary
lesson: 14404
title: Overarm
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how something is done. Overarm means done with the arm raised above the shoulder. «Sam threw the ball overarm, high over the net.» His arm went up above his shoulder to throw it.
explain: Overarm can describe a noun, as in «an overarm throw», or tell how something is done, as in «Priya bowled overarm». Its opposite is underarm, where the arm stays low.
explain: Check the meaning with context. «Lee bowled overarm and the stumps flew.» The clue is bowled, a throw in cricket, so overarm must describe how he threw. Swap in "with the arm raised above the shoulder" and the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Overarm means thrown or done with the arm raised above the shoulder.
fact: «An overarm throw» goes further in PE than a throw made with a low arm.
fact: In cricket, bowlers can bowl overarm.
fact: In swimming, front crawl uses overarm strokes.
fact: The opposite of overarm is underarm.
exercise: «Sam threw the ball overarm, high over the net.» What does overarm mean? | With the arm kept low by the hip | *With the arm raised above the shoulder | Very slowly and gently | With one foot off the ground
exercise: Which word is the opposite of overarm? | Sideways | Backwards | *Underarm | Overtime
exercise: In «an overarm bowl», what kind of word is overarm? | Preposition, because it shows place | Verb, because it shows an action | *Adjective, because it describes the bowl | Noun, because it names a thing
test: «Lee bowled overarm in the match.» What does overarm tell you about the bowling? | How many runs he scored | *How he bowled: with the arm raised above his shoulder | Where the ball landed | Who was watching
test: Mia says overarm and underarm mean the same. Is she right? | Yes, but only in swimming | *No, they are opposites: the arm is raised high for overarm and kept low for underarm | No, but only in cricket | Yes, they mean exactly the same thing
exam: «The overarm throw went further than the underarm throw.» What does overarm mean in this sentence? | Thrown with the arm kept low | Thrown while running | Thrown by a very old player | *Thrown with the arm raised above the shoulder
